- id: Q-22
  severity: high
  status: closed 2026-09-06 dissolved by SEMANTICS.md (owner: "proof requires demonstrandum"): proven = the demonstrandum's lock is discharged; grounded/anchored are descriptors of the demonstrandum and never gate status; "counts against a Millennium problem" is the registry lock relation
  title: what "anchored" must mean for proven
  detail: >
    Two computed properties now exist per custom constant. ANCHORED: a
    checked Iff/Eq chain to a Mathlib-named declaration (strong fidelity;
    available for Riemann only among the seven). GROUNDED: the
    definitional closure ends in the pinned libraries with nothing hidden
    (available for all seven, and also for the induction-template control's private
    predicate, which is a grounded def). The status rule today caps a
    claim at `stated` unless every custom constant is ANCHORED, which
    leaves six Millennium problems unreachable by any proof at this pin.
  options: >
    A (current): keep the Iff rule; six problems dead at this pin.
    B (recommended): `proven` requires GROUNDED for every custom constant;
    ANCHORED is recorded as a separate fidelity field; "counts against a
    Millennium problem" stays a lock relation (registry_match, or a
    checked Iff to a registry lock). Consequence: the induction-template control N1
    computes `proven` as the implication it is, with `step` listed under
    hypotheses and registry_match none; the mismatch is then caught by the
    lock relation and the generated label (Q-5), not by a status. N1's
    calibration requirement changes accordingly and Q-1 gets its rule
    (conditional = proven with explicit Prop hypotheses that name claim
    ids or are not discharged).
