- id: Q-25
  severity: medium
  status: open
  title: exit condition 6 (proposals attempted as `A ↔ B`) is vacuous over theorem pairs
  detail: >
    lemma's S5 proposals (L-5) pair two Mathlib THEOREMS A, B, both proven at
    the pin. Any two proven closed propositions are equivalent — `⟨fun _ => B,
    fun _ => A⟩` discharges `A ↔ B` — and the same holds pointwise under shared
    binders (`∀ xs, P xs ↔ Q xs`, since both P xs and Q xs hold). The self-proof
    gate (exit condition 2) cannot catch this: the Iff has its own lock, and A
    and B are legitimately usable constants. "Discharged" would measure the
    ladder finding two existing proofs, not an equivalence. Missed in design
    review (ATTEMPTS.md rev 2 exit condition 6; lemma docs/prover-loop.md).
    Found 2026-09-11 while preparing the attempt form; nothing was run.
  fix: >
    Pending the user's call (doctrine change). Proposals must pair
    propositions whose truth is NOT already established: the sides of
    Mathlib Iff theorems (corpus fields iff_lhs / iff_rhs; the pairs S5 was
    trained on), Prop-valued definitions, or hypotheses. The demonstrandum for
    sides L_i, L_j drawn from different Iff theorems with α-equivalent binder
    telescopes is `∀ xs, L_i xs ↔ L_j xs`; a discharge is a new fact even when
    it chains through the source Iffs (record the used constants as a
    difficulty feature, do not exclude them). lemma's proposal generator and
    the L-5 rerank move to that pool; until then exit condition 6 is blocked
    and no `A ↔ B` run is made.
